# QNEthernet comes from a fork, and has to: upstream's master carries no
# IEEE 1588 support at all, the 2022 branch this one is built on is no
# longer served by upstream, and the servo calls two methods that exist
# nowhere else. README.md, "Why QNEthernet comes from a fork", has the
# detail. Time is upstream's own.
[submodule "libraries/QNEthernet"]
	path = libraries/QNEthernet
	url = https://github.com/JaumeAP/QNEthernet.git
	branch = multicast-ttl
[submodule "libraries/Time"]
	path = libraries/Time
	url = https://github.com/PaulStoffregen/Time.git
